   "id": 521543,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In some primroses, the petal color blue is dominant. A cross between a true-breed blue primrose and a white primrose yields progeny with white petals. A second gene at another locus prevented the expression of the dominant coat color. This is an example of ______.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1019972,
     "content_html": "codominance"
    },
    {
     "id": 1019973,
     "content_html": "hemizygosity"
    },
    {
     "id": 1019974,
     "content_html": "incomplete dominance"
    },
    {
     "id": 1019975,
     "content_html": "epistasis"
    }
   ],
